---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import { APP } from '../links'
---

<Base
  title="Oh Hi markdown"
  description="An ordinary markdown editor over a vault of plain .md files, with a relay: your own notes stay local, and a shared folder is edited together, live."
>
  <h1>Remove the barrier between personal and collaborative notes.</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Oh Hi is an ordinary markdown editor over a vault of plain <code>.md</code> files,
    <strong>with a relay</strong>. Your own notes stay local. Share a folder when you want company,
    and edit it together, live, without conflicts.
  </p>
  <p class="callout">
    <strong>Early days.</strong> Oh Hi is in daily use by the team that builds it, and it is not
    finished.
  </p>
  <p class="actions">
    <a class="button primary" href={APP}>Open in your browser</a>
    <a class="button" href="/download">Download for macOS and Linux</a>
  </p>

  <hr />

  <section>
    <h2>What it is</h2>
    <ul class="points">
      <li>
        <strong>An editor</strong> over a vault of plain <code>.md</code> files. Open it over your
        existing notes. Wikilinks, tags, frontmatter, daily notes &amp; collections.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>A relay</strong>, a small service that sits between you and others. Share a folder
        through it and whoever holds the link edits it with you, live, without conflicts.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Agents</strong>, in the app and outside it. Inside, an agent edits alongside you
        once you choose a provider: cloud, local or self-hosted. Outside, the <code>ohhi</code>
        command and its MCP server give any agent the same vault.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>
